cmdline.txt.append.disabled forces a display the headless rpi4 lacks (both HDMI connectors read
`disconnected`, so weston's DRM backend has no output). `video=HDMI-A-1:1920x1080M@60D` drives the
connector with no EDID, like a dummy plug, on the real vc4/v3d GPU. A run made this way proves the
path, not a comparable number: the mode is invented, and results record `display_forced`.

It is disabled because a forced mode with nothing attached can hang vc4's probe, and so the boot;
an armed stick that hangs is chosen again on every power cycle, these images carry no `panic=`, and
the rpi4 has no console. Enable it on the SD system first, where the stick stays an unarmed
fall-through, and on the stick only once that has booted: drop the `.disabled` suffix.
